{
  "an7.66:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.66 ",
  "an7.66:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an7.66:0.3": "The Seven Suns ",
  "an7.66:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an7.66:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī in Ambapālī’s Mango Grove. ",
  "an7.66:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "an7.66:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "an7.66:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "an7.66:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an7.66:2.1": "“Mendicants, conditions are impermanent. ",
  "an7.66:2.2": "Conditions are unstable. ",
  "an7.66:2.3": "Conditions are unreliable. ",
  "an7.66:2.4": "This is quite enough for you to become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed regarding all conditions. ",
  "an7.66:3.1": "Sineru, the king of mountains, is 84,000 leagues long and 84,000 leagues wide. It sinks 84,000 leagues below the ocean and rises 84,000 leagues above it. ",
  "an7.66:3.2": "There comes a time when, after a very long period has passed—many years, many hundreds, many thousands, many hundreds of thousands of years—the heavens fail to rain. ",
  "an7.66:3.3": "When this happens, the plants and seeds, the herbs, grass, and big trees wither away and dry up, and are no more. ",
  "an7.66:3.4": "So impermanent are conditions, ",
  "an7.66:3.5": "so unstable, so unreliable. ",
  "an7.66:3.6": "This is quite enough for you to become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed regarding all conditions. ",
